1
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:16,015
‎Gyro Zeppeli finishes!

2
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:20,937
‎We have our first stage champion!

3
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:31,823
‎Gyro, you really took first…

4
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,492
‎The key to his victory

5
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:36,828
‎was that Spin!

6
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,956
‎Well done, Valkyrie.

7
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:43,293
‎I have to win this race, you know.

8
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:46,796
‎I'll be counting on you.

9
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:49,632
‎Gyro Zeppeli…

10
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:53,303
‎I hear he's kept his identity
‎a complete secret.

11
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,305
‎Authorities say

12
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:59,601
‎he came to the US
‎from Genoa, Italy, this May.

13
00:01:01,019 --> 00:01:02,686
‎He's a foreigner?

14
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:05,689
‎Yes. Apparently, he came aboard a ship

15
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,817
‎owned by a European imperial family.

16
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,569
‎Mr. Steel!

17
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,863
‎A decision has been reached!

18
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:14,074
‎Why?

19
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:17,493
‎How could this happen?

20
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:21,790
‎I'm supposed to be
‎the one-in-five-billion lucky guy!

21
00:01:22,373 --> 00:01:24,458
‎I'm not in first…

22
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,876
‎Damn it.

23
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,253
‎I, Dio…

24
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:31,381
‎Would you like some food?

25
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,134
‎It's free for all competitors.

26
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:37,055
‎Looks like the guy at the start.

27
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,140
‎But a different one?

28
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:41,601
‎I'll take some.

29
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,065
‎Just as you said.

30
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,442
‎First off, congratulations.

31
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,528
‎Thanks.

32
00:01:52,529 --> 00:01:54,947
‎But how can you be so carefree?

33
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,616
‎You're a competitor too.

34
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,494
‎Ladies and gentlemen,
‎thank you for waiting!

35
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:03,372
‎Here are the first stage standings!

36
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:06,793
‎After careful deliberation, the winner is,

37
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:10,629
‎Saddlecloth number 990,

38
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,756
‎Sand Man!

39
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,526
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

40
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:47,893
‎#02 THE SHERIFF'S REQUEST
‎TO MOUNTAIN TIM

41
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:48,977
‎The winner? Him?

42
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:50,979
‎Wasn't Gyro first?

43
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,689
‎Quiet, please!

44
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:55,567
‎Our balloon observers confirmed
‎that Gyro Zeppeli

45
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,779
‎used a weapon
‎to interfere with another competitor!

46
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:02,491
‎It happened at the downhill's end,
‎just before the final turn!

47
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:03,826
‎The downhill?

48
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,247
‎That part!

49
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:13,585
‎Therefore, Gyro Zeppeli
‎receives a twenty-place penalty!

50
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:16,381
‎Everyone below him moves up accordingly!

51
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:19,384
‎Diego's in second!

52
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:21,594
‎Pocoloco's in third.

53
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:25,764
‎More importantly,
‎Mountain Tim took fourth!

54
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:28,559
‎He got his horse's nose across the line!

55
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,771
‎What's wrong, Slow Dancer?

56
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:34,440
‎Mountain Tim…

57
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:38,611
‎A legendary cowboy
‎renowned throughout the Old West.

58
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:41,239
‎I've heard the stories.

59
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:45,827
‎They say every horse
‎bows its head to him out of respect.

60
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:58,840
‎Mr. Steel, congratulations
‎on a successful first stage.

61
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:00,716
‎Thank you.

62
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:02,135
‎When's the next stage?

63
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,944
‎Got something to say, Mr. Zeppeli?

64
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:22,487
‎You should've been disqualified.

65
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:24,115
‎You interfered using a weapon.

66
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:30,495
‎No complaints.

67
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:33,081
‎What's done is done.

68
00:05:33,082 --> 00:05:35,752
‎No point arguing about it now.

69
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,545
‎I just came here

70
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:41,132
‎to blow off some steam for tomorrow.

71
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:44,427
‎You go celebrate with your champagne.

72
00:05:45,344 --> 00:05:46,554
‎Hey, wait!

73
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:51,642
‎What?

74
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,648
‎What's going on?

75
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:01,402
‎I had all that champagne
‎imported from France!

76
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:12,079
‎What's happening?

77
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,289
‎Mr. Steel.

78
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,083
‎Sheriff?

79
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:18,168
‎May I have a word?

80
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,796
‎It's a private matter.

81
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,799
‎I'm feeling a little better now.

82
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:27,470
‎So you coming along for the next stage?

83
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,388
‎Johnny Joestar.

84
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:33,935
‎Of course. I'm going to beat you.

85
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,145
‎Very well.

86
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:41,901
‎Lesson two is:
‎don't let your muscles know.

87
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,152
‎Listen.

88
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:47,240
‎The tighter you grip your arm like this,

89
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:51,326
‎the more your muscles sense the force
‎and try to resist it.

90
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:54,412
‎Your body instinctively
‎tries to protect itself

91
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:56,623
‎because your muscles detect it.

92
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,501
‎That's how every living body works.

93
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:01,628
‎The Spin never lets the muscles know.

94
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:02,964
‎Control the skin.

95
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:07,300
‎As long as it's only skin-deep,
‎the muscles won't know.

96
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:09,928
‎Control the skin? What do you--

97
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:12,264
‎Want to try? If you're game.

98
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:16,269
‎The champagne cork in your hand
‎is already spinning.

99
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:33,535
‎That's how you get off a horse.

100
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:35,913
‎The horse's muscles never knew.

101
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:40,459
‎That movement
‎used the opposite spin from when I got on.

102
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,127
‎Don't let the muscles know.

103
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:45,840
‎The weapon isn't the Steel Ball itself.
‎It's the power of the Spin.

104
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:50,051
‎Johnny Joestar, we'll cross
‎the desert in the second stage.

105
00:07:50,052 --> 00:07:51,971
‎It's over 700 miles.

106
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,848
‎It's going to be tough.

107
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:56,725
‎Let's form an alliance.

108
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,479
‎We'll finish one-two!

109
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,400
‎I'll be the one, though.

110
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:11,615
‎What is this?

111
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:16,244
‎As you can see,
‎there's been a murder, Mr. Steel.

112
00:08:16,245 --> 00:08:19,456
‎Someone murdered them during the race.

113
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:23,043
‎Over 3,000 competitors
‎were riding alongside them,

114
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:25,170
‎yet no one saw a thing.

115
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:28,632
‎Don't be ridiculous!
‎What possible motive--

116
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:31,134
‎The motive? 50 million dollars.

117
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:33,054
‎To move up in the standings.

118
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:37,224
‎Every competitor is a suspect.

119
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:39,601
‎At this rate, there'll be more victims.

120
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:43,231
‎Will you suspend the race
‎while we investigate?

121
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:45,774
‎No!

122
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:50,279
‎This race has grown beyond my own will.

123
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,447
‎I thought as much.

124
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:54,909
‎Steven. You're…

125
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:02,416
‎Their scent has a calming effect.

126
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:06,754
‎Please accept them, Mrs. Steel.

127
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:17,181
‎I understand how concerned you are
‎for your beloved husband.

128
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,767
‎Rest assured. Leave it to me.

129
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:25,855
‎Is he Mountain Tim?

130
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:27,232
‎What's he doing here?

131
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:29,859
‎I sent for him

132
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:32,362
‎to track down the killer.

133
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:33,446
‎Track the killer?

134
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:35,740
‎But he's a competitor!

135
00:09:35,741 --> 00:09:37,326
‎That is why.

136
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:40,954
‎He could be the killer's next target.

137
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:43,582
‎In that case, let him track the killer.

138
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,417
‎You sure ask a lot of a man.

139
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:50,338
‎Mr. Steel, I'd like to appoint him
‎as my deputy.

140
00:09:50,339 --> 00:09:52,758
‎Only if that's acceptable to you.

141
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,471
‎This is terrible.

142
00:09:58,139 --> 00:10:02,226
‎I can't even think about winning
‎with someone like this around.

143
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:06,731
‎A lot of my friends
‎are racing in this too.

144
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:14,822
‎If I'm tracking footprints,
‎this is the one.

145
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,951
‎This one must be the most aggressive.

146
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:22,537
‎The horseshoe has a V-shaped chip
‎in the center.

147
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,831
‎What?

148
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:26,166
‎The horse was agitated.

149
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:28,294
‎Because it saw human blood.

150
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:32,423
‎The rider's methodical.
‎Must've been raised in the desert.

151
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:35,176
‎A bottle beside the victim?

152
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,429
‎There's something inside.

153
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:41,599
‎Is that a button?

154
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:52,651
‎Does it have something to do
‎with the murder?

155
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,528
‎It's from the victim's jeans.

156
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,781
‎Why did the button come off

157
00:10:57,782 --> 00:11:00,034
‎and end up inside the bottle?

158
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,077
‎One thing's certain.

159
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:07,583
‎It's dangerous to let anyone get close
‎without knowing who they are.

160
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:16,967
‎SEPTEMBER 26, 1890
‎SANTA MARIA NOVELLA CHURCH

161
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:20,637
‎Five minutes to the start!

162
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:25,351
‎The second stage is
‎a long-distance race of roughly 750 miles.

163
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,728
‎It should take about two weeks.

164
00:11:28,729 --> 00:11:31,856
‎From here, they'll cross
‎the Arizona desert

165
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:33,776
‎and finish at Monument Valley.

166
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:36,820
‎As long as they pass the checkpoints,

167
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:39,240
‎their routes are entirely up to them!

168
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:43,828
‎Gyro, Sand Man's the favorite
‎to win this stage.

169
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,746
‎The betting's on. He's the favorite.

170
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:47,998
‎What do you think?

171
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,708
‎Not me?

172
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,043
‎Afraid not.

173
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:54,504
‎For the record, I'm sixth.

174
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:56,256
‎And you're ninth.

175
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,258
‎What do they know?

176
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:00,677
‎The general public.

177
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:03,138
‎Not that I care.

178
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,557
‎Mountain Tim, over there…

179
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:08,852
‎He's a favorite to win too.

180
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,311
‎There you go.

181
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:13,022
‎He's got a funny hat.

182
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:14,899
‎Makes me want to stomp on it.

183
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:18,945
‎Before it's even off his head.

184
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:23,033
‎They say Mountain Tim isn't cut out
‎for short races because he's a cowboy.

185
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:26,327
‎But yesterday, he caught me by surprise.

186
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:28,079
‎Then passed me before the finish.

187
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,498
‎With a hat like that?

188
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:33,793
‎And you didn't notice him? Ha, ha! Nyo-ho!

189
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,921
‎Gyro, I think this stage

190
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,757
‎will be a battle to find water.

191
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:44,180
‎In 1875, a cavalry unit of 26 men
‎was wiped out.

192
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:47,850
‎Not in battle, and not by accident.

193
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:51,979
‎The usual watering hole
‎dried up that year.

194
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:56,357
‎They wandered the endless desert
‎in search of water.

195
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:58,277
‎They slowly baked to death

196
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:01,280
‎in the scorching heat.

197
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:05,242
‎This marks a watering hole.

198
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:09,370
‎Day one, the first watering hole
‎isn't until mile 30.

199
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:11,372
‎If we can't find it,

200
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,459
‎we won't just retire. We'll die.

201
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:17,295
‎And this cork…

202
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:19,632
‎How can I make it spin?

203
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:27,223
‎It's time for the second stage to begin!

204
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,517
‎They're off!

205
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:33,312
‎The Steel Ball Run's second stage
‎is under way!

206
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:36,814
‎-What?
‎-He's pulling away!

207
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:40,194
‎That's Gyro! Gyro Zeppeli!

208
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:43,738
‎What's his problem?

209
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:46,617
‎Didn't he hear what I just said?

210
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:51,622
‎I'm coming! I'm right behind you!

211
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,334
‎No way…

212
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:58,503
‎What's Gyro Zeppeli doing?

213
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:01,297
‎He's not just taken off.
‎He's changed his route!

214
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:02,632
‎The desert?

215
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:06,679
‎Is he cutting straight across
‎and ignoring the watering hole?

216
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:09,138
‎Are you crazy, Gyro?

217
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:11,432
‎We've got another 750 miles ahead of us!

218
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:12,893
‎What are you thinking?

219
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:17,063
‎We're rivals, remember?

220
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:19,942
‎Wanna come? I'm taking the shortest route.

221
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:22,151
‎Why wouldn't I?

222
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,903
‎Otherwise, Sand Man

223
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:25,990
‎or someone else will beat us.

224
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,032
‎Damn it!

225
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,492
‎Wow!

226
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:32,537
‎Gyro's not alone!
‎Other competitors are following him

227
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:33,955
‎into the desert!

228
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:37,208
‎No sane competitor
‎would choose that route!

229
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,795
‎Do they have a death wish?

230
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:59,315
‎There are no railroad tracks
‎beyond this point.

231
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,983
‎The train will go on ahead

232
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:04,236
‎and wait at the checkpoints.

233
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:08,115
‎6 HOURS LATER

234
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:10,159
‎Who's that?

235
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,911
‎What's hanging from his ear?

236
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,830
‎I can't tell through the dust.

237
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:19,335
‎According to his saddlecloth number,
‎his name's Robinson.

238
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,129
‎He's about 150 lengths behind us.

239
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:24,505
‎Hey, Gyro.

240
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:26,382
‎We've been riding for six hours.

241
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,718
‎We're still headed the right way, right?

242
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:31,220
‎50 miles to the watering hole.

243
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:33,599
‎Sorry to keep asking,
‎but are we still right?

244
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:39,980
‎There isn't any mountain like that
‎on this map.

245
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:48,864
‎Yep! We're right on course.
‎Everything's perfect!

246
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,866
‎-Probably.
‎-What?

247
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:54,202
‎Did you just say "probably"?

248
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,371
‎Don't worry.

249
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:59,457
‎Other competitors are following us.
‎We're right!

250
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:01,751
‎-I think.
‎-"I think"?

251
00:16:01,752 --> 00:16:04,045
‎We'll die if we miss that watering hole!

252
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:08,633
‎I'm asking if you know anything
‎about the desert!

253
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,927
‎I'm telling you, we're fine.

254
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:13,013
‎Out here, close enough is good enough.

255
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:17,100
‎More importantly,
‎have you mastered the Spin?

256
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:19,561
‎The cork spin I taught you!

257
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:39,455
‎What's wrong?

258
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:41,542
‎Something just flew by.

259
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:46,212
‎Gyro…

260
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:48,465
‎Your ear…

261
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,351
‎This is…

262
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:02,270
‎Shit! My arms got cut!

263
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:05,190
‎It's ahead!
‎Something's coming from up ahead!

264
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:12,697
‎He's on the move.
‎He's trying to catch up to us!

265
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,408
‎Was it him? Did he do this?

266
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:16,743
‎Calm down, Gyro.

267
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:18,494
‎Something's wrong.

268
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:20,413
‎The attack came from ahead.

269
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:22,206
‎Get behind those rocks.

270
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:24,250
‎Don't move the horses too much.

271
00:17:24,251 --> 00:17:27,253
‎Gyro, these are cactus spines.

272
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,464
‎You know a lot about the desert?

273
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,965
‎A little.

274
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:34,135
‎Some desert cactuses shoot their spines.

275
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:35,637
‎They're called chollas.

276
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,930
‎When an animal gets close,

277
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,934
‎they sense vibrations
‎and fire their spines.

278
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,981
‎Damn. Those must be chollas.

279
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:48,983
‎They're growing all over the place.

280
00:17:48,984 --> 00:17:51,778
‎So which is it?

281
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:55,199
‎Are we the ones at fault
‎for riding into this cactus patch?

282
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:58,910
‎Or is he the bad guy,

283
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:01,162
‎using the cactuses against us?

284
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,455
‎I don't know.

285
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:06,293
‎You'd have to get pretty close
‎to make a cholla fire its spines.

286
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,503
‎He's much too far away.

287
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:11,757
‎But he's definitely got a motive.

288
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:17,221
‎He can use the cactuses to take us out
‎without penalty.

289
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,722
‎He's coming around!

290
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:21,933
‎But we don't know if he did it.

291
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:24,685
‎Damn it!
‎We've got to get out of this area.

292
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,187
‎Let's ride, Johnny!

293
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,606
‎Right! Gyro!

294
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:33,402
‎The reins were cut!

295
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:35,989
‎No way! They cut the reins!

296
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,243
‎It's impossibly accurate!

297
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:50,545
‎Get on your horse!

298
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,548
‎This is definitely his doing!

299
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:00,138
‎Go on ahead!

300
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,891
‎Blood got in my eyes,
‎but my eyes are fine!

301
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,934
‎Go!

302
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:07,645
‎We promised
‎we'd make it to the finish together,

303
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,188
‎but a race is a race.

304
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,898
‎Don't wait for me.

305
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:13,277
‎I'll catch up once I wipe the blood off!

306
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:19,073
‎All right. I'll go on ahead.

307
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:20,242
‎Yeah! Go!

308
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:21,827
‎But…

309
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:25,747
‎I'm heading toward that bastard!

310
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:35,923
‎Gyro! Your Steel Ball
‎is considered a weapon!

311
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:38,593
‎And there's no proof he's behind this.

312
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:42,555
‎If you attack him now,
‎you'll be disqualified!

313
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:45,766
‎You should just get out of this area!

314
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:48,645
‎You should just stay in the race!

315
00:19:55,736 --> 00:20:00,239
‎In one desert village, whenever a dispute
‎turned into a fight to the death,

316
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:04,369
‎the loser would be chained to a cactus
‎and left there to die.

317
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:07,038
‎I grew up in a village like that.

318
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:10,083
‎I mastered a skill
‎so no one could ever control me.

319
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:14,379
‎To make sure I never lose,
‎I keep insects inside my body.

320
00:20:15,339 --> 00:20:17,924
‎Using the airflow
‎from their high-speed flight,

321
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:21,887
‎I can shoot cholla spines
‎exactly where I want!

322
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,851
‎Now that you know my secret,

323
00:20:28,852 --> 00:20:30,144
‎take this.

324
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:33,522
‎No one is getting ahead of me
‎in this race!

325
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:34,399
‎Nyo-ho!

326
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:38,277
‎Then we're thinking along the same lines.

327
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:41,322
‎You thought I just dropped my Steel Balls?

328
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:44,785
‎My precious Steel Balls on the ground?

329
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:50,122
‎What's that buzzing?

330
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:53,877
‎It's not my insects, is it?

331
00:20:54,461 --> 00:20:57,505
‎I'm not that accurate.

332
00:20:57,506 --> 00:21:00,216
‎But the Spin's vibrations reached you.

333
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:02,636
‎They spread through the ground around you.

334
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:06,723
‎I'll keep my distance.
‎Don't wanna get caught in that.

335
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:18,860
‎It wasn't me.

336
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:23,949
‎The cactus did it.

337
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:27,869
‎That cost us more time than I expected.

338
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:31,373
‎Come on, Johnny. Let's get moving.

339
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,543
‎Right. Gyro.

340
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:12,390
‎That's…

341
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:14,893
‎Robinson.

342
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:19,605
‎It's not him.

343
00:23:19,606 --> 00:23:22,024
‎The killer I'm after

344
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:23,652
‎has a different horseshoe.

345
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:26,404
‎But I'm still on the right trail.

346
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,408
‎The chipped horseshoe
‎came through here already.

347
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:33,328
‎About 30 minutes ago, I'd say.

348
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:35,914
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
